::ENG4_U05_L06_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG4.W.04] Sentences: A. This evidence shows why the proposal is practical. B. The report lists three cities that reduced costs. C. The proposal is practical because similar plans have succeeded elsewhere. What is the strongest order? {
=A. C, B, A.#Correct. This order moves from claim to evidence to explanation.
~B. A, B, C.#Incorrect. The explanation appears before the main claim.
~C. B, A, C.#Incorrect. The claim should come before evidence.
~D. A, C, B.#Incorrect. The paragraph begins with explanation before the claim.
}
::ENG4_U05_L06_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG4.L.01] Draft: The data is current. However, it supports the claim. Which transition best replaces However? {
~A. However.#Incorrect. However signals contrast, but the second sentence supports the first.
=B. Therefore.#Correct. Therefore signals a result or conclusion.
~C. Instead.#Incorrect. Instead signals replacement, not support.
~D. Meanwhile.#Incorrect. Meanwhile signals time or simultaneous action.
}
::ENG4_U05_L06_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG4.V.03] In revision, what does coherent mean? {
~A. full of unrelated details.#Incorrect. That is incoherent, not coherent.
~B. grammatically incorrect.#Incorrect. Coherence concerns logical connection.
=C. logically connected and easy to follow.#Correct. Coherent writing fits together clearly.
~D. intentionally confusing.#Incorrect. Coherent writing is clear.
}
::ENG4_U05_L06_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG4.W.04] Which revision best improves organization? {
~A. Add a random transition before every sentence.#Incorrect. Transitions must match the logic.
~B. Put evidence, explanation, and claim in any order.#Incorrect. Order affects clarity.
~C. Remove all transitions and evidence.#Incorrect. That weakens organization.
=D. Begin with the main idea, then present evidence, then explain its significance.#Correct. This creates logical progression.
}
::ENG4_U05_L06_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG4.L.01] Draft: The study was large therefore the results were more reliable. Which revision best clarifies the relationship? {
=A. The study was large; therefore, the results were more reliable.#Correct. The semicolon and transition correctly connect the ideas.
~B. The study was large therefore the results were more reliable.#Incorrect. This lacks punctuation between clauses.
~C. The study was large, therefore the results were more reliable.#Incorrect. A comma alone is not enough before therefore between independent clauses.
~D. The study large therefore reliable results.#Incorrect. This is not standard English.
}
